# These two golang.org/x/crypto vulnerabilities are fixed in 0.56.0,
# but that requires go 1.26.0. According to govulncheck, the vulnerabble
# code is not called by CAPI anyway, so we can ignore these for now.
CVE-2026-56855
CVE-2026-78662

# These golang.org/x/net vulnerabilities (GO-2026-6611, GO-2026-6612 and
# GO-2026-6617 in govulncheck) are fixed in 0.60.0, but that requires
# go 1.26.0. They affect the HTTP/2 server in golang.org/x/net/http2,
# which CAPI does not use.
# Also see .govuln_exclude.
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-78663
CVE-2026-97032

# These golang.org/x/net vulnerabilities (GO-2026-6603 and GO-2026-6610 in
# govulncheck) are fixed in 0.60.0, but that requires go 1.26.0.
# CVE-2026-78659 affects the HTTP/2 server, which CAPI does not use.
# CVE-2026-78660 affects the HTTP/2 client and can only be triggered by a
# malicious server, which is not reasonable to defend against.
# Also see .govuln_exclude.
CVE-2026-78659
CVE-2026-78660
